---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {datasetEntries,datasetSchema,childrenRows,snapshotDate,scopeNote,snapshot,rawSnapshot,snapshotExportRevision,snapshotPublicationRevision,snapshotAmount,snapshotGross,required,citations,exportDate,treeManifestChecksum} from '../../../lib/discovery';
export function getStaticPaths(){return datasetEntries.map(entry=>({params:{gov:entry.slug},props:{entry}}));}
const {entry}=Astro.props;
const root=required(entry.root),rows=childrenRows(entry.root),sources=citations([root]);
const category=`tree/${entry.slug}/_root.json`;
---
<Base title={entry.name} description={`${entry.period}. Browse and download the sourced 2026 budget tree in integer cents; see coverage, version and qualifications.`}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(datasetSchema(entry))} />
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/datasets/">Datasets</a> / {entry.name}</nav>
  <section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Versioned public data</p><h1>{entry.name}</h1><p class="lede">{entry.period}. Published snapshot root amount: <strong>{snapshotAmount(entry.root)}</strong>. <a href={`/${entry.slug}/`}>Browse the interactive tree</a>.</p></section>
  <p>{entry.qualification} {scopeNote}</p>
  <h2>Coverage and provenance</h2><dl><dt>Geography</dt><dd>{entry.coverage}</dd><dt>Period and basis</dt><dd>{entry.period}; {root.basis}.</dd><dt>Published snapshot export</dt><dd><time datetime={snapshotDate}>{snapshotDate}</time>, according to the <a href={`${snapshot}/site/manifest.json`}>download snapshot's site manifest</a>. This is a data-build date, not the source publication date. The interactive site's export may be newer.</dd><dt>Source/export revision</dt><dd><code>{snapshotExportRevision}</code> (earlier commit recorded in the published manifest; it does not contain the complete published snapshot).</dd><dt>Immutable publication revision</dt><dd><code>{snapshotPublicationRevision}</code> (contains the complete release and anchors these download links).</dd><dt>Units and schema</dt><dd>Amounts are integer cents (<code>amount_cents</code>). Stable <code>id</code> and <code>parent_id</code> describe hierarchy. <code>basis</code>, <code>period_label</code>, <code>note</code> and source indices describe evidence. Tree lookup links IDs to complete records and citations in site chunks.</dd></dl>
  <h2>Explore top-level categories</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Selected category rows from the current interactive site export (<time datetime={exportDate}>{exportDate}</time>), amounts in dollars; these may differ from the published download snapshot</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(({node,url,amount})=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={url}>{node.name}</a></th><td>{amount}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  {entry.slug==='city'&&<p>Published snapshot City gross appropriation: {snapshotGross}. The <a href="/city/counted-twice">cross-fund counted-twice view</a> is separate from the net root, not an additional government budget.</p>}
  {entry.slug==='parks'&&<p>{root.note} See its <a href="/parks/">budget tree</a>.</p>}
  <h2>Download and verify</h2><ul><li><a href={`${rawSnapshot}/${category}`}>Download root JSON</a> (<code>{category}</code>)</li><li><a href={`${rawSnapshot}/tree/manifest.json`}>Download category manifest</a></li><li><a href={`${rawSnapshot}/tree/lookup.json`}>Download complete box-ID lookup</a></li><li><a href={`${snapshot}/catalog.json`}>SHA-256 file checksums and original paths</a></li></ul><p>The catalog checksum for <code>tree/manifest.json</code> is <code>{treeManifestChecksum}</code>. Use the catalog for checksums of other files. <a href="https://github.com/gettty/chicagobudget/blob/main/data/README.md">Schema and download guide</a>.</p>
  <h2>Official source and terms</h2><p>These citations come from the current interactive export; consult the pinned snapshot's site chunks and tree lookup for the exact published download's source indices.</p><ul>{sources.map(source=><li><a href={source.url}>{source.label}</a></li>)}</ul><p>This is a transformed independent dataset, not an official government publication. Original source terms are retained and not broadly relicensed. See <a href="https://github.com/gettty/chicagobudget/blob/main/LICENSES.md">source terms</a> and <a href="/sources">all citations</a>. <a href="/guides/">Read explanatory guides</a>.</p>
</Base>
<style>code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }</style>
